From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 18:58:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: Add the USB3 combo PHY

Add the node of the first combo PHY in the SERDES block, which carries
the SuperSpeed lanes of the USB3 controller, and the SERDES top page it
shares with the second combo PHY as a system controller.

The top page has no reset or clock of its own in the node: its reset
is the SERDES bus reset, which the PHYs and the SERDES CCU share, and
the PHYs hold it deasserted before they touch the page.

A kernel whose combo PHY driver still maps the top page as its own
register region does not bind the PHY with this device tree.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards; the PHY node binds
through the SERDES top syscon on both, and on one board the USB3
controller enumerates a stick through it.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
index 66f3532a1954..f1830bc73230 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
@@ -761,6 +761,24 @@ serdes_ccu: clock-controller@6c00000 {
 			#reset-cells = <1>;
 		};
 
+		combophy0: phy@6c01000 {
+			compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-usb3-combophy";
+			reg = <0x06c01000 0x1000>,
+			      <0x06c80000 0x20000>;
+			reg-names = "link", "pma";
+			allwinner,serdes-top = <&serdes_top>;
+			clocks = <&ccu CLK_SERDES_PHY>, <&rtc CLK_HOSC_SERDES0>;
+			clock-names = "serdes", "hosc";
+			resets = <&ccu RST_BUS_SERDES>;
+			#phy-cells = <0>;
+			status = "disabled";
+		};
+
+		serdes_top: syscon@6c06000 {
+			compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-serdes-top", "syscon";
+			reg = <0x06c06000 0x1000>;
+		};
+
 		r_ccu: clock-controller@7010000 {
 			compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-r-ccu";
 			reg = <0x07010000 0x230>;
